The Windows installer bundles a Python runtime and these libraries, each under its own licence:
- CPython (Python Software Foundation License, https://www.python.org)
- NumPy (BSD-3-Clause, https://numpy.org)
- matplotlib (matplotlib License, based on the PSF licence, https://matplotlib.org), with its
  dependencies: contourpy, cycler, fonttools, kiwisolver, packaging, pillow, pyparsing,
  python-dateutil and six (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0, HPND or PSF licences)
- DejaVu fonts shipped with matplotlib (Bitstream Vera / DejaVu licence)
The way the runtime is packed, unpacked on first start and driven is copied from Datum Plot.

The window bundles SolidJS (MIT, https://www.solidjs.com) and the IBM Plex fonts
(SIL Open Font Licence 1.1).

The built-in materials data (data/*.json) is our own compilation of public values. Every value
names its source in data/sources.json; those sources keep their own terms. No proprietary
materials database was used.

